                    {
                        "sense_id": "021690e1-5989-30ef-b6ab-e5918365a2e7",
                        "entry_id": "0a98ad78-4c79-3f41-b1ff-0b5ed41e4ff5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to the Egyptian god Set"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a573c66-ef53-4410-9ade-a05bd23ae1b7",
                                "sense_id": "021690e1-5989-30ef-b6ab-e5918365a2e7",
                                "text": "But if these hippopotami are Sethian, how could Apophis, a professed follower of Seth, allow this to go on in his own city of Avaris?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ceedf03a-7028-4fb2-9d33-e2fa60aec4ae",
                                "sense_id": "021690e1-5989-30ef-b6ab-e5918365a2e7",
                                "text": "At any rate this shows that Sekhemib-Peribsen certainly did not pass into history as a Sethian schismatic or heretic."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98e0b98e-2fa1-4cb4-8053-e34552a59ab8",
                                "sense_id": "021690e1-5989-30ef-b6ab-e5918365a2e7",
                                "text": "Associated with Horus: in the Late Period the nome-sign is often written with a falcon (Horus) on the back of an oryx, which itself was a Sethian animal."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
